1
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:06,967
(Penny:)Wow, Sheldon, I cannot believe
you made up your own game.

2
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:10,842
(Sheldon:)Oh. Research Lab is more than a game.

3
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:12,261
It's like the slogan says:

4
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:16,519
"The physics is theoretical,
but the fun is real."

5
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:19,682
(Leonard:)We must not be playing it right.

6
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:24,694
(Penny:)All right. Five.
One, two, three, four, five.

7
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:26,108
(Penny:)Oh, wow, look at that.

8
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:29,116
My Department of Defense
research grant is renewed.

9
00:00:29,279 --> 00:00:30,949
Oh. Great roll.

10
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:33,864
(Sheldon:)Now you can demolish
your Soviet-style cyclotron...

11
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:37,034
(Sheldon:)...and build the large hadron collider.

12
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:39,083
(Penny:)Yay.

13
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:41,202
(Sheldon:)You're a natural at this, Penny.

14
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:44,004
(Sheldon:)And as the first beta testers,
you two have quite the edge...

15
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:46,919
(Sheldon:)...when we play with Wolowitz
and Koothrappali on Sunday.

16
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:51,048
(Leonard:)Oh, gee, Sheldon,
I don't think we can play on Sunday.

17
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:52,467
(Sheldon:)Why not?

18
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:56,555
(Leonard:)Because of the reasons
that Penny will now tell you. Penny?

19
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:59,063
(Penny:)I have to pick up my friend Justin
from the airport.

20
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:01,565
(Leonard:)There you go.
She has to pick up her friend Justin.

